From d1f80aad4ec1a65a288f8f840aab03f9237761f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hibreak <hibreak@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 13:17:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SystemUI: e-ink lock screen clock and sleep screen (always-on
 display)

With debug.sysui.eink_palette:
- The lock screen clock is pure black on a light lock wallpaper and white
  on a dark one, from the wallpaper dark-text hint (patch 0010 rule),
  instead of the clock seed or accent colour.
- Always-on display is the sleep screen: the lock screen as it is, on the
  lock wallpaper. No black front scrim, no blanking, and no light reveal
  scrim (it covered the panel in black in AOD, and in white when the
  screen turned off). The panel keeps its image without power.
- While dozing, the clock, the notification icons and the battery line
  keep their lock screen colours instead of turning white.
- No burn-in offsets or scaling: e-ink can not burn in, and each shift
  would cost a panel refresh.

Change-Id: Ib81ca76095ed46dc00b429b4dc3805fc16d5721a
